{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggxLgopYJUQUWSYbTTP8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For MnBr₂, using a standard approximate strong-field d⁵ model, I get **Dq ≈ 199 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 1 990 cm⁻¹), B ≈ 626 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3 350 cm⁻¹ (C/B ≈ 5.3)**. The small Dq should be treated with caution (see the last section).\n\n**Approach**\n\nHigh-spin octahedral Mn²⁺ has a ⁶A₁g ground state, so the three observed bands are spin-forbidden transitions to quartet states. I used the second-order expressions for the three quartets, written with x = 10Dq. These are the commonly quoted Orgel-type approximations. I did not diagonalise the full Tanabe–Sugano d⁵ matrices.\n\n- ⁴T₁(G): E = 10B + 6C − x − 26B²/x\n- ⁴T₂(G): E = 18B + 6C − x − 38B²/x\n- ⁴E, ⁴A₁(G): E = 10B + 5C (this level does not depend on the field)\n\n**Solving**\n\n1. From the ⁴E band: 10B + 5C = 23 000, so C = 4 600 − 2B.\n2. Subtracting the ⁴T₁ equation from the ⁴T₂ equation gives 8B − 12B²/x = 2 650. Rearranged, x = 12B² / (8B − 2 650).\n3. Putting C into the ⁴T₁ equation gives x + 2B + 26B²/x = 8 360.\n4. I solved steps 2 and 3 together by trial values of B:\n   - B = 625 gives a left-hand side of 8 336.\n   - B = 626 gives 8 355.\n   - B = 626.3 gives 8 361.\n   - So B ≈ 626 cm⁻¹.\n5. Then x = 10Dq ≈ 1 994 cm⁻¹, so Dq ≈ 199 cm⁻¹.\n6. And C = 4 600 − 2(626.3) ≈ 3 350 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Caveat about Dq**\n\nB and C are well fixed, mainly by the field-independent ⁴E band and the gap between the two T states. The Dq value is much less reliable. It comes entirely from the second-order expressions, which are approximate. The model is also very sensitive here because the high-spin d⁵ bands depend only weakly on Dq. For a bromide, 10Dq ≈ 2 000 cm⁻¹ is smaller than typically expected for Mn²⁺. Fitting with the full Tanabe–Sugano d⁵ matrices would likely give a noticeably larger Dq.\n\n{\"Dq\": 199, \"B\": 626, \"C\": 3348, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Solved approximate second-order d5 quartet-band expressions; the small Dq is model-sensitive.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":816,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":816,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b998ce3-c524-4411-a2e3-5ce9bff1544c","uuid":"c26c06c3-0a52-494e-96aa-a06fe78e77a7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:39:05.371Z","request_id":"req_011CggxLgQkgAdYwvA5VoVmR"}
